A||N||15||RoadRocket||Force Balancer Assembly||||5||
Z||000000||RoadRocket||10-08-2001||10:02 PM||||Last week, I had the steering on my 88 fixed. While the mechanic was doing it, I asked him to investigate the rattling noise that was coming from the engine.<P>He said it was the Force Balancer assembly. That it could go anytime, without warning, and that it could take the engine with it.<P>So I thought to myself, OK, no big deal. I've been playing with the idea of replacing the stock 4 banger VTech engine with a 6 banger one. If I loose the engine, I'll have an excuse to replace it now.<BR>Of course, the flip side of this argument is: I live in Phoenix. If the engine fails in the city, no problem. But if it fails in the country, problem... The middle of nowhere Arizona can be a very bad place, indeed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>So, do I replace it now? And hold on to my stock vtech engine a little longer? Or do I wait for it to fail, and replace it then?<P>And if I replace it now, when I finally replace the engine, will I have to replace the force balancer, as well? Is it dependent on the engine?<P>Thoughts?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-08-2001||10:46 PM||||Maybe your Muffler Bearing is bad.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>Force balancer?  Harmonic balancer?<BR>When do you hear the noise? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||10-08-2001||11:52 PM||||Don't laugh at him too much, Joe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The 87 and 88 4 cylinders indeed have a device called a "force balancer".  It has 2 balance shafts in it along with the oil pump and is driven off of a large gear cast into the crankshaft.  I've never had the pleasure of having to work on one, but I can see how it could cause a noise if the bushings that the shafts ride in are getting very worn.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||10-09-2001||12:16 AM||||Sorry...never heard of that one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||10-09-2001||12:18 AM||||double post!<p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||10-09-2001||12:28 AM||||I would go ahead and replace it with a new assembly. That way you won't get stranded out in the middle of the great big nothing! That is, if you think that the engine is worth it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||10-09-2001||07:56 PM||||Sorry, Vtech!?? Stock?||||reg||11
Z||000007||theogre||10-09-2001||08:09 PM||||It could be the balance unit.... just as likely it could be anything....<P>that motor is common to a number of GM cars. You can get another one easy enough. cost about 200-300$ at nearly any salvage yard. Souldn't take more than a day or two to swap.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||10-09-2001||08:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>If the engine fails in the city, no problem. But if it fails in the country, problem...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I see it the other way around. I don't even like driving through the city, but being stranded there...that's just scary! ||||reg||7
Z||000009||Steve Normington||10-09-2001||09:44 PM||||Don't know if this will help, but I've got a complete cradle assembly (engine, tranny, cradle, shafts, and knuckles) from an 84 MT. If you want it, its yours for free. Just get it out of my yard.<P>PS. The V-6's don't have the force balancer.||||reg||1
Z||000010||RoadRocket||10-09-2001||09:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>that motor is common to a number of GM cars. You can get another one easy enough. cost about 200-300$ at nearly any salvage yard. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>But if I replace the engine, Ogre, I'm not likely gonna put another 4banger in it. I'll probably replace with a v6. I'm leaning towards the 3800 Series II.<P>Which is why I am debating about fixing the 4banger, as opposed to replacing it now. I've already spent thousands on the Fiero this year. I don't know if I want to spend thousands more.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
