Z||000012||RoadRocket||10-09-2001||10:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>Don't know if this will help, but I've got a complete cradle assembly (engine, tranny, cradle, shafts, and knuckles) from an 84 MT. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you mean 84 GT, Steve?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Might take you up on it concerning the tranny. <P>Someone correct me if I'm wrong, but my model has a 3 speed transmission. (I think.)<P>My understanding of the 3800 Series II engine says it requires a 4 or 5 speed engine.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
